 <a id="client-references"></a>
 ## Client references
 
+An adapter whose accepted operation can finish without producing input returns `SessionPromptValue.noInput` only after authoritative terminal proof of successful operation and no input. A no-input fact alone proves neither success nor absence of side effects. Its branded request and original projection identify the optimistic echo; generic acceptance supplies neither fact. `SessionFace.settleSubmissionNoInput` consumes the same proof after a lost reply or later recovery, independently of draft hydration or revision changes. It retires only that echo with `reason: 'no-input'`, preserves successful acceptance, creates no inbox or history record, and never sends input. Observed inbox or durable input takes precedence over a contradictory no-input proof. Repeated settlement of an absent echo has no effect; an original in-flight prompt retains its own settled record to recognize a late matching receipt. Disposal and mismatched identity cannot authorize execution or affect a successor echo. An embedding must keep unknown outcomes explicit and validate the native proof before invoking this method.
+
 `@deepseek-ai/dsh-api-session-controller/projection` exposes the React-free `parseProjectionBinding`, `projectionSource`, and `projectionGeneration` decoders to providers; decoding validates opaque identity, while authenticated source authority remains the provider’s responsibility.
 
 Opt-in `projectionRebuild: true` separates disposable presentation from the exact retained execution binding. `binding.projection` reports rebuilding, ready, or failed with a generation cancellation signal. Typed control invalidation names the next branded source/generation; duplicate and retired invalidations are ignored. A fresh journal, complete projections, and mandatory assistant baseline commit at one cut. Every page and projection writer must carry that identity; stock providers reject scoped reads. Old rows withdraw immediately, failed baselines stay visibly failed, and `sessions.retryProjection(id)` retries only the last authority. A terminal control failure withdraws scoped presentation before cancellation callbacks; retry explicitly recreates the Session-owned observer, accepts its complete control baseline, then opens the presentation baseline. Concurrent retries share observer recovery; old callbacks cannot publish and final release cannot resurrect a scope. It does not use physical reconnect as projection reset or change Gateway stream semantics. Stop, Agent Contexts, pending Interactions, and independent retains keep their lifetimes. Staging allows 512 combined baseline/update entries and 4 MiB of UTF-8 JSON for `{ baseline: baselineOrNull, updates: [[key, { value, seq }], ...] }`, including the complete baseline identity/cut, keys, sequences, wrappers and separators. These are serialized payload limits, not JavaScript heap limits; 256 retired generations per Client lifetime prevent authority replay, then require a visible reload failure. Defaults retain stock reconnect and pagination behavior.
